<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jayavarman II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/802">802 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jayavarman II was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> ruler who in 802 CE proclaimed himself universal monarch, or chakravartin, in a ceremony declaring independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>. His reign is traditionally regarded as the foundation of the Khmer Empire. He established the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devaraja">devaraja</a> cult of kingship.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Sdok Kak Thom inscription of 1053 records that <b>Jayavarman II</b> and his son Indrayudha defeated a Cham army in 790 before moving north of the Tonlé Sap to found Hariharalaya.</blockquote><a href="/empire/chenla">Chenla · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Its foundation is traditionally dated to 802 CE, when <b>Jayavarman II</b> underwent a consecration ritual on Mount Mahendraparvata, the Phnom Kulen plateau, proclaiming himself a universal monarch (chakravartin), inaugurating the cult of the devaraja and symbolically freeing the land from the overlordship of “Java”.</blockquote><a href="/empire/khmer-empire">Khmer Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Khmer prince <b>Jayavarman II</b> spent years at the Shailendra court before returning around 790 to rule as devaraja and proclaim independence from Java in 802, founding the Angkor era.</blockquote><a href="/empire/medang-kingdom">Medang Kingdom · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Since <b>Jayavarman II</b> proclaimed himself chakravartin, “universal ruler”, and devaraja, “god-king”, in 802, Khmer kings were held to have the divine quality of living gods, incarnations of Shiva or Vishnu.</blockquote><a href="/societies/khmer-empire">Social Hierarchy of the Khmer Empire</a></li><li><blockquote>Its territories were absorbed into the Khmer Empire after <b>Jayavarman II</b> proclaimed his rule in 802, and many historians doubt that the Chinese division matched clear political boundaries.</blockquote><a href="/state/land-chenla">Land Chenla</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Jayavarman II</b>, who had spent time in Java, returned to unite the Khmer lands and in 802 proclaimed himself universal monarch, ending the division and founding the Khmer Empire.</blockquote><a href="/state/water-chenla">Water Chenla</a></li></ul></section>
